// marklid.peg — normative grammar for the markl-id text form (RFC 0011
// "Markl ID Format")
//
// SYNC OBLIGATION: this grammar MUST remain in sync with this
// repository's RFC 0011 (docs/rfcs/0011-markl-id-format.md) —
// specifically §2 (Structure), §2.1 (ABNF Grammar), §2.3 (Quoted
// Digest Slot), and §3 (Blech32 Encoding). If RFC 0011 amends those
// sections, update this file to match.
//
// RFC 0011 was formerly madder RFC 0002; it moved here to complete the
// piggy#183 markl-ownership inversion, and was renumbered only because
// piggy's 0002 slot already holds the PIV-ECDH box format. Its internal
// section numbers are unchanged, so citations of "RFC 0002 §2.1" still
// land on the right text. The spec is now IN THIS REPOSITORY, upstream
// of its own implementation — an earlier version of this comment sent
// readers downstream to madder, and that misdirection caused a real
// sequencing error (linenisgreat/madder#273).
//
// Notation: Ford PEG, authored langlang-compatible (cutting-garden FDR
// 0022): // comments only, explicit spacing, no automatic space
// insertion. Validate with BOTH -disable-builtins AND -disable-spaces
// (hyphence#7 dialect-gap finding: -disable-builtins alone only drops
// the injected Spacing/EOL/EOF rule DEFINITIONS; the separate
// whitespace-injector pass, gated by -disable-spaces, still auto-
// inserts Spacing calls between sequence items unless both flags are
// given).
//
// Whitespace: a markl-id's BARE form has no whitespace anywhere (RFC
// 0011 §2.1, §2.2). Whitespace can appear only INSIDE a quoted slot
// (`"my thing"@blake2b256-...`), never between the slots and never
// around the '@' or '-' joins. That is why no rule below calls a
// Spacing production.
//
// EXPORT SURFACE (piggy#236): this file is the ROOT of the ecosystem's
// grammar-composition chain (piggy → trellis → hyphence; papi consumes
// validators). Downstream grammars stage it via the flake output
// `.#marklid-grammar` and `@import` named rules individually. The
// following rule names are therefore a FROZEN CONTRACT — renaming or
// restructuring any of them is a breaking change for downstream
// importers, and TestGrammarImportSurface (markl_registrations) is the
// gate that says so:
//
//   String, Char             — the quoting productions (owned here;
//                              trellis imports and drops its copy)
//   FormatData, Format, Data — the digest-slot productions
//   PurposeBare, PurposeChar — the bare purpose production
//
// Scope: structural (context-free) shape only. Does NOT and per PEG
// CANNOT encode: blech32 checksum validity (§3.3, a BCH computation —
// see §4.1), payload-size-matches-format (§5, a registry lookup),
// purpose/format compatibility (§6.1, a registry lookup), or the
// rejection of a quoted digest slot (§2.3, a validation-time refusal of
// a shape this grammar deliberately admits). Those stay the Go/Rust
// reference decoders' job (go/internal/bravo/markl, crates/piggy-markl)
// — a grammar-valid string can still be semantically rejected
// downstream; that's expected, matching 0014-trellis.peg's own
// "groundness is semantic, not grammar" precedent.

MarklId        <- ((Purpose '@')? FormatData)? EOF

// purpose (RFC 0011 §2.1): an ASCII-inclusion identifier, or a quoted
// String for anything outside it. NARROWED 2026-07-20
// (linenisgreat/madder#273 ruling 1) from the former "any Unicode code
// point except '@' and whitespace", which superseded in turn the
// earlier system-domain-role-version convention (madder#270,
// piggy#219).
//
// The inclusion list is deliberate, not a transcription of trellis's
// Ident: trellis's IdentRune is EXCLUSION-style (any rune that is not
// Reserved and not whitespace), and adopting it would have narrowed
// piggy by only the ~16 reserved characters rather than by the amount
// asked for. Inclusion also makes both slots ASCII-inclusion (Format is
// already [a-zA-Z0-9_]) and keeps a bare markl-id safe to paste into
// shell, URL, and log contexts, where a bare '(', ';', or '&' is a
// hazard.
//
// CONSEQUENCE (RFC 0011 §2.1): this REVOKES madder#270's bare-Unicode-
// pinnability. A purpose spells a pinned object's id, so a Unicode- or
// punctuation-named object is no longer bare-pinnable — it is pinned
// QUOTED: `"café/naïve"@blake2b256-...`. The quoted alternative answers
// #270's concern rather than ignoring it.
//
// Purpose ⊂ trellis Ident: every string matching PurposeBare is a valid
// trellis identifier, but not conversely. RFC 0011 §7.4's divergence
// register asserts that SUBSET invariant, not equality.
Purpose        <- PurposeBare / String
PurposeBare    <- PurposeChar+

// '-' is written LAST so it is a literal hyphen, not a range endpoint.
PurposeChar    <- [a-zA-Z0-9_/-]

// format-data (RFC 0011 §2.1, §2.3): the bare two-slot digest form, or
// a quoted String. The quoted alternative is an EXTENSION POINT — it
// PARSES into a dedicated value and is REFUSED at validation until a
// concrete meaning is specified (§2.3, ruling 11). This mirrors
// trellis's own precedent for `~=` and the typed closure `-[p]->>`:
// the shape parses, validation says no. Admitting it here costs
// nothing, because every form usable TODAY still goes through
// FormatDataBare and keeps that production's structural guarantees.
FormatData     <- FormatDataBare / String

// The two-slot structure is retained deliberately (ruling 3). A generic
// bare token was rejected: this structure is the ONLY thing rejecting
// `blake2b256` (no data at all), `blake2b256-9bt3...` ('b' outside the
// blech32 alphabet), and truncated payloads.
FormatDataBare <- Format '-' Data

// format = 1*( ALPHA / DIGIT / "_" ), RFC 0011 §2.1. Structurally open,
// semantically registered (ruling 4): any such token PARSES, and the
// registry decides validity at decode time. Registering a new format
// therefore never touches this grammar and never forces a downstream
// re-import.
Format         <- FormatChar+
FormatChar     <- [a-zA-Z0-9_]

// data: >=7 chars (1+ payload + 6-char checksum) from the 32-char
// blech32 alphabet, LOWERCASE ONLY (RFC 0011 §3.5, ruling 6). This
// narrows bech32's all-lower-or-all-upper rule: bech32 permits
// uppercase to enable QR alphanumeric mode, but that mode's charset
// (0-9, A-Z, space, $%*+-./:) has no lowercase, no '@', and no '_', so
// a markl-id can never be QR-alphanumeric-encoded regardless of payload
// case. The uppercase allowance buys markl-ids nothing.
Data           <- DataChar DataChar DataChar DataChar DataChar DataChar DataChar DataChar*
DataChar       <- [qpzry9x8gf2tvdw0s3jn54khce6mua7l]

// Doddish quoting rules: double or single quotes; backslash escapes
// \n \t \r \a \b \f \v, \" and \\ round-trip; unknown escapes pass the
// following character through unchanged. Quoting is permitted on BOTH
// slots (ruling 2).
//
// PIGGY OWNS String/Char (piggy#236, grammar-composition ruling
// 2026-07-22: every grammar unit gets exactly one home, composed
// upstream→downstream via langlang @import). These productions
// originated as a copy of 0014-trellis.peg's String — that relationship
// is now INVERTED: trellis imports them from this file and drops its
// local copy. The rules stay semantically "Doddish quoting" (dodder's
// shipping scanner discipline); what changed is which file is the
// definition and which is the import.
String         <- '"' (!'"' Char)* '"'
                / "'" (!"'" Char)* "'"
Char           <- '\\' . / .

EOF            <- !.

// ---- conformance vectors (each MUST parse under MarklId) ----------
//
//   (empty string)
//     — the null-state text form (RFC 0011 §2)
//   blake2b256-9ft3m74l5t2ppwjrvfg3wp380jqj2zfrm6zevxqx34sdethvey0s5vm9gd
//     — a bare digest, no purpose
//   dodder-blob-digest-sha256-v1@blake2b256-9ft3m74l5t2ppwjrvfg3wp380jqj2zfrm6zevxqx34sdethvey0s5vm9gd
//     — a registered purpose (RFC 0011 §6.1); this grammar treats it
//       identically to a general one — registration is a semantic,
//       not structural, distinction (RFC 0011 §6)
//   one/uno@blake2b256-9ft3m74l5t2ppwjrvfg3wp380jqj2zfrm6zevxqx34sdethvey0s5vm9gd
//     — a general/unregistered, `/`-bearing purpose (piggy#219)
//   md@blake2b256-9ft3m74l5t2ppwjrvfg3wp380jqj2zfrm6zevxqx34sdethvey0s5vm9gd
//     — a short general purpose
//   "my thing"@blake2b256-9ft3m74l5t2ppwjrvfg3wp380jqj2zfrm6zevxqx34sdethvey0s5vm9gd
//     — a quoted purpose carrying whitespace, which the bare form
//       cannot spell (ruling 2). The digest slot stays OUTSIDE the
//       quoting, structurally intact (RFC 0011 §2.2)
//   "café/naïve"@blake2b256-9ft3m74l5t2ppwjrvfg3wp380jqj2zfrm6zevxqx34sdethvey0s5vm9gd
//     — how a Unicode-named object is pinned now that the bare form is
//       ASCII-closed (RFC 0011 §2.1; supersedes madder#270)
//   "a@b"@blake2b256-9ft3m74l5t2ppwjrvfg3wp380jqj2zfrm6zevxqx34sdethvey0s5vm9gd
//     — a quoted purpose carrying '@' (RFC 0011 §2.2, piggy#227).
//       Quoting is the escape mechanism, so it must be able to carry
//       the rune most in need of escaping; the bare form still excludes
//       '@' entirely. NOTE the join here is the SECOND '@' — decoders
//       MUST locate it with a quote-aware scan, never with the first
//       '@'. 0014-trellis.peg's MarklTerm comment has always said this;
//       the two specs now agree.
//
// ---- parses here, REJECTED at validation (RFC 0011 §2.3) ----------
//
//   md@"blake2b256-9ft3m74l5t2ppwjrvfg3wp380jqj2zfrm6zevxqx34sdethvey0s5vm9gd"
//     — a quoted digest slot. Structurally admitted as an extension
//       point (ruling 11); the reference decoders MUST refuse it until
//       a concrete meaning is specified. A grammar gate asserting this
//       string PARSES is asserting the extension point exists, NOT that
//       the id is usable.
//
// ---- rejected shapes (each MUST NOT parse under MarklId) ----------
//
//   blake2b256
//     — missing "-data" (no separator)
//   my thing@blake2b256-9ft3m74l5t2ppwjrvfg3wp380jqj2zfrm6zevxqx34sdethvey0s5vm9gd
//     — whitespace in a BARE purpose; spell it "my thing"@... instead
//   café@blake2b256-9ft3m74l5t2ppwjrvfg3wp380jqj2zfrm6zevxqx34sdethvey0s5vm9gd
//     — non-ASCII in a bare purpose (madder#273 ruling 1); spell it
//       "café"@... instead
//   a.b@blake2b256-9ft3m74l5t2ppwjrvfg3wp380jqj2zfrm6zevxqx34sdethvey0s5vm9gd
//     — '.' is outside the bare purpose charset, though it IS a legal
//       trellis IdentRune; this is the Purpose ⊂ Ident gap in action
//   dodder-blob-digest-sha256-v1@blake2b256-9bt3m74l5t2ppwjrvfg3wp380jqj2zfrm6zevxqx34sdethvey0s5vm9gd
//     — 'b' is outside the blech32 alphabet (charset violation in data)
//   BLAKE2B256-9FT3M74L5T2PPWJRVFG3WP380JQJ2ZFRM6ZEVXQX34SDETHVEY0S5VM9GD
//     — uppercase data; lowercase only (RFC 0011 §3.5, ruling 6)
